WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.360
- [Instructor] What we have here

00:00:01.360 --> 00:00:03.410
are pictures of running pigs,

00:00:03.410 --> 00:00:06.220
and we can try to figure out
how many running pigs there are

00:00:06.220 --> 00:00:08.280
by just counting the pigs,

00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:10.820
but we're gonna start
building some new muscles

00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:12.830
and this muscle's going to involve,

00:00:12.830 --> 00:00:16.750
hey, if we group the pigs
into equal groupings,

00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:19.670
can that help us figure out
how many pigs there are?

00:00:19.670 --> 00:00:22.820
And you can see that I
have groupings of seven.

00:00:22.820 --> 00:00:26.900
Each of these groups
are seven running pigs,

00:00:26.900 --> 00:00:29.130
so how many total groups do I have?

00:00:29.130 --> 00:00:32.930
Well, I have one, two, three groups

00:00:32.930 --> 00:00:35.300
of seven running pigs each.

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:37.330
Three equal groups.

00:00:37.330 --> 00:00:39.340
If I said, what's the total
number of running pigs

00:00:39.340 --> 00:00:40.820
that I'm dealing with?

00:00:40.820 --> 00:00:45.440
Well, I have three sevens,
three groups of seven, and so,

00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:49.200
that's the same thing as
seven plus seven plus seven,

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:50.800
and if you wanted to
figure out what that is,

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:51.910
you could skip count.

00:00:51.910 --> 00:00:56.360
If we skip count by seven,
we go seven then 14 then 21,

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:01.430
and so, three sevens, which is
seven plus seven plus seven,

00:01:01.430 --> 00:01:04.480
is 21, so there's 21 pigs here,

00:01:04.480 --> 00:01:05.960
and you can verify on your own

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:09.910
that if you count this, you
will indeed see 21 pigs.

00:01:09.910 --> 00:01:11.183
Let's do another example.

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:15.200
Here, I'm looking at a picture
of a bunch of blue seals,

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:17.800
not something that you are
likely to see in the wild.

00:01:17.800 --> 00:01:20.640
And these blue seals have,
once again, been grouped.

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:21.640
Let's see how many groups there are.

00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:26.640
There are one, two, three,
four, five, six, seven groups,

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:29.700
and how many are in each group?

00:01:29.700 --> 00:01:32.040
Well, we could see that
they're all groups of

00:01:32.040 --> 00:01:33.730
one, two, three, four, five.

00:01:33.730 --> 00:01:35.710
They're equal groups.

00:01:35.710 --> 00:01:36.840
What are dealing with?

00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:39.730
Well, we're dealing with
seven groups of five,

00:01:39.730 --> 00:01:44.140
so I could write seven groups of five.

00:01:44.140 --> 00:01:47.200
I could write seven fives.

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:52.200
I could write five plus
five plus five plus five

00:01:52.950 --> 00:01:57.950
plus five plus five plus five,
so that is seven fives there.

00:01:58.390 --> 00:01:59.940
And if I wanted to
figure out where that is,

00:01:59.940 --> 00:02:00.810
I could skip count.

00:02:00.810 --> 00:02:03.000
I could skip count seven fives,

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:08.000
so that'd be five, 10, 15, 20, 25, 30, 35.

00:02:11.220 --> 00:02:12.650
If I were to add all these fives up,

00:02:12.650 --> 00:02:15.250
five plus five is 10, add
another five, you get to 15.

00:02:15.250 --> 00:02:16.490
Add another five, 20.

00:02:16.490 --> 00:02:17.630
Add another five, 25.

00:02:17.630 --> 00:02:18.550
Add another five, 30.

00:02:18.550 --> 00:02:22.203
Add another five, 35, which
is exactly what you see there.

00:02:23.290 --> 00:02:26.320
We're starting to see that
sometimes grouping things

00:02:26.320 --> 00:02:29.950
can help us appreciate how
many things there are there.

00:02:29.950 --> 00:02:31.030
And I know what some of
you all are thinking,

00:02:31.030 --> 00:02:33.410
well, hey, couldn't I just count things?

00:02:33.410 --> 00:02:34.740
Well, you could,

00:02:34.740 --> 00:02:37.650
but what if you had 100 groups of five?

00:02:37.650 --> 00:02:38.540
Well then, it's gonna take you

00:02:38.540 --> 00:02:40.150
a little bit more time to count.

00:02:40.150 --> 00:02:42.130
But the techniques that we're building

00:02:42.130 --> 00:02:43.680
will help you one day be able to

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:46.403
think about those things quite easily.

